-- title:
--   Top-window stability of truncated logarithm covectors
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$, and suppose $\mathcal{O}$ carries an algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly the ideal $(p)$. Let $F$ be a commutative $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal{O}$, i.e. a $d$-tuple of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in both blocks, satisfying associativity and, by the `IsComm` hypothesis, invariance under swapping the two blocks of variables. Let $Fp$ be a $d$-tuple of power series in the same variables with vanishing constant terms such that for every $i$ and every $m \neq 0$ one has $\mathrm{coeff}_m(Fp_i)\cdot p = p^{\deg m}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_i)$ (so $Fp$ is $p^{-1}$ times the $p$-rescaling of $F$), where $\deg m$ is the total degree. Let $\varphi$ be a $d$-tuple of power series in $d$ variables with vanishing constant terms, whose linear part (the matrix of coefficients of the $X_j$) is the identity, such that for every $N$ and $i$ all but finitely many coefficients of $\varphi_i$ lie in $(p^N)$, and satisfying the functional equation $\varphi_i \circ Fp = \varphi_i(X_{\mathrm{inl}}) + \varphi_i(X_{\mathrm{inr}})$ for all $i$. Fix $i$ and natural numbers $E$, $w$. The assertion is that there is $N_1$ such that for all $N_1 \le N \le M$ the following holds. Let $c_N, c_M : (\mathrm{Fin}\,d \to_0 \mathbb{N}) \to \mathcal{O}$ be families such that for each $m$: if $\deg m \le N$ then $c_N(m) = p^{N-\deg m}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$, and if $\deg m > N$ then either $c_N(m)\,p^{\deg m - N} = \mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$ or $c_N(m) = 0$ and $p^{\deg m - N}$ does not divide $\mathrm{coeff}_m(\varphi_i)$; and likewise for $c_M$ with $M$ in place of $N$. Let $\ell_N, \ell_M$ be Witt vectors over the ring of power series $\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ whose ghost components realise these families in the sense that $\mathrm{coeff}_{m'}(\mathrm{ghost}_n(\ell_N)) = c_N(p^{N-1-n}\, m')$ for all $n < N$ and all $m'$, and $\mathrm{coeff}_{m'}(\mathrm{ghost}_n(\ell_M)) = c_M(p^{M-1-n}\, m')$ for all $n < M$ and all $m'$. Then for every $j$ with $N - w \le j < N$ (truncated subtraction), $$\ell_M.\mathrm{coeff}(j + (M-N)) - \ell_N.\mathrm{coeff}(j) \in (p) + (X_1,\dots,X_d)^E .$$
--
--   This is the comparison, in the top $w$ positions, of the Witt-vector components carrying the truncated logarithm covectors of a commutative formal group law at two precisions $N \le M$: after the shift by $M-N$ they agree modulo $(p)$ together with the $E$-th power of the ideal generated by the variables. It is used in the construction of the covector-valued logarithm map on the finite level, being cited by [`Deformation.truncate_map_mem_wittHom_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector`](thm.html#Deformation.truncate_map_mem_wittHom_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector).
